meta {
  name: Update Profile
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

patch {
  url: {{base_url}}/account/update-profile
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{access_token}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "first_name": "علی",
    "last_name": "رضایی"
  }
}

docs {
  ## Purpose

  Partially updates the basic profile information of the authenticated user.

  ## Authentication

  Requires a valid access token.

  ## Behavior

  - Only fields included in the request body are updated.
  - Omitted fields remain unchanged.
  - At least one supported field must be provided.
  - Supported fields include `first_name`, `last_name`, and `mobile`. To change `mobile`, first request verification for the new number, then send that same number with the received `otp`. An unchanged mobile does not require an OTP.
  - Names are trimmed and limited to 1,000 UTF-16 code units each, the same limit used by registration and user management.
  - An omitted or blank name leaves that field unchanged; blank names do not clear existing values.
  - A supplied non-string (including `null`) or over-limit name rejects the whole request with `400`; no profile field is written.
  - Users do not have individual language preferences.
  - Username and email are managed through their dedicated endpoints.

  ## Response

  - `200 OK` — Profile updated successfully.
  - `400 Bad Request` — The request body is empty or contains invalid values.
  - `401 Unauthorized` — The access token is missing, invalid, or expired.
  - `413 Payload Too Large` — The JSON body exceeds 64 KiB, including when `Content-Length` understates its actual size.
  - `415 Unsupported Media Type` — The request does not use `application/json`.
  - `429 Too Many Requests` — Mobile-change confirmation attempt limit reached (including a supplied unchanged mobile).
}
